# Line endings are a property of this project, not of the machine that clones it.
#
# Every generator under tools/ writes LF. Git's system-level core.autocrlf=true
# checked text files out as CRLF, so 8,786 tracked files differed from their own
# blobs by one byte per line and nothing else. That silently broke level 6 of the
# validation ladder -- source-to-shipping equality -- because a byte-equality
# check cannot tell a re-encoded file from a re-authored one: check_deepworks
# reported 414 drifting models, check_material_textures a drifting texture and
# check_fey_generation a drifting quest chapter, and not one character of content
# had changed in any of them.
#
# Pinned here so a fresh clone on any machine holds the bytes the generators emit.

*                   text=auto eol=lf

# Windows batch is the one text format that genuinely wants CRLF, and every
# gradlew.bat in first_party_mods/ ships that way.
*.bat               text eol=crlf
*.cmd               text eol=crlf

# Binary. Git's heuristic classifies all of these correctly today; declaring it
# makes it a contract rather than a lucky NUL sniff of the first 8 KB. A CRLF
# pass over an .nbt or an .mca is not a defect anyone notices until a structure
# fails to place or a world will not load.
*.png               binary
*.nbt               binary
*.mca               binary
*.dat               binary
*.dat_old           binary
*.jar               binary
*.zip               binary
*.docx              binary
*.pyc               binary
*.sqlite            binary
*.sqlite-shm        binary
*.sqlite-wal        binary
*.ogg               binary
*.gz                binary
